{
  "family": "Barlow Condensed GO",
  "source": {
    "kind": "hmtx",
    "date": "2026-10-29",
    "fonts": [
      "Barlow Condensed Regular / Bold (Office CloudFonts cache, static TTFs)",
      "LiberationSans"
    ],
    "probe": "hmtx advance-ratio buckets (<= 3 % span); Word paces the cloud face at its own advances (production PDF spans / hmtx = 0.994 over 112 lines)"
  },
  "note": "Barlow Condensed is an M365 cloud font Word downloads and lays out with its real\nadvances (unlike the Bahnschrift variable instances, which Word paces at Calibri-class\nwidths). Without the face Chromium drew Helvetica, 1.35x wider, wrapping every table\ncell (corpus 2026-10-29). Faces are advance-ratio buckets over Liberation Sans (Word\nadvance / base advance per Latin-1 glyph, greedy buckets no wider than 3 %, one\nsize-adjusted face per bucket, the rangeless face at the lowercase ratio); within\n0.5 % on 57 Word lines where per-class faces missed by up to 2.8 %. The cloud cache\nhas no italic cut; Word obliques the upright, so the italic faces reuse the upright\nratios. Glyph height shrinks with the width (a known compromise of size-adjust);\nline pitch stays the hhea 1.2 from word-faces.json.",
